    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-08T09:56:02+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-08T09:56:02+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T23:26:02Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-07T23:26:02Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred south of SA will continue to drift eastwards, while a weak low pressure system and trough in WA move east across the SA border. The high will drift southeast of Tasmania by Monday, while the trough and low drift eastwards across SA, clearing to the east late Tuesday. Another high will develop south of the state on Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds east to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h decreasing to 25 to 35 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 29 to 38.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:20am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers east of Ceduna in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and early afternoon. The chance of raised dust east of Ceduna in the late morning and afternoon. Winds northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h in the morning then tending south to southwesterly in the early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower west of Ceduna, near zero chance elsewhere. Winds south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h tending south to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to around 14 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 26.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloud clearing. Winds southerly 15 to 25 km/h turning southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching 22 to 27.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
